# ADR and documentation

## Statement classes

Label each claim as one of: **evidence**, **proposal**, **decision**,
**assumption**, **unresolved policy**. Do not convert a suggestion into a fact.

Do not invent business policy. Do not treat a suggested deployable count as an
architectural fact. Deployable grouping is decided by ADR, not by folder layout.

## ADRs

Use [docs/adr/0000-template.md](../../docs/adr/0000-template.md). Every ADR must
include:

- Context
- Options considered
- Decision drivers
- Decision (or explicit `proposed` / unresolved outcome)
- Consequences
- Migration impact
- Observability
- Security
- Rollback
- Unresolved questions

Status `accepted` is required before implementation that depends on the decision.
`prepare-adr` must not silently mark unresolved policy as accepted.

## Canonical docs

Update [architecture/invariants.md](../../architecture/invariants.md),
[architecture/service-boundaries.yaml](../../architecture/service-boundaries.yaml),
and [architecture/ownership-matrix.yaml](../../architecture/ownership-matrix.yaml)
instead of adding a conflicting parallel statement. Link ADRs from
[docs/adr/README.md](../../docs/adr/README.md).
